      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T20:21:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional nit: Creating screenshots usually happen during development of a feature. Some features may require a specific setup that can not be easily set up from a fresh installation. One example is that if a feature requires a sign-in user, then it might be easier to reuse the installed app with its existing state. Chrome also supports an experiment feature where it can take a `--enable-features` parameters, or force variant configuration if a feature relies on a variant. So, adding an option like skip install might help to use existing configuration from what the user already has in simulator.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 94,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 67
      },
      "revId": "c52f35035c3b7423055b27ed1b6276c3a15b8aa8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
